From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Project Luma <engineering@projectluma.org>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 13:01:29 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] wayland: Tell who a client is

meta_wayland_client_get_identity() looks a client up once, from what the
kernel says about the connecting process: sandboxed (a Flatpak's
.flatpak-info and its application ID, a Snap AppArmor label, the Luma
capsule SELinux domain luma_application.process read with SO_PEERSEC, a
Luma closure application's app-luma-*.scope), the Shell's own (a client
Mutter started, or Mutter itself), or a host client, named by the
desktop-file ID of its app-*.scope or else its executable. A process that
cannot be inspected counts as sandboxed. The process start time comes with
it.

Mutter has no wp_security_context_v1, and capsules reach the display
socket directly, so the peer's credentials are what can be trusted here.
---
 src/meson.build                           |   2 +
 src/wayland/meta-wayland-client-sandbox.c | 336 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 src/wayland/meta-wayland-client-sandbox.h |  58 ++++
 3 files changed, 396 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 src/wayland/meta-wayland-client-sandbox.c
 create mode 100644 src/wayland/meta-wayland-client-sandbox.h

